# Git commits

[Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/). No other style.

```text
<type>: <subject>

<body>
```

- Subject ≤ **50** characters, 72 absolute max. Imperative, no period.
- Body (and footer) wrap at **72** columns. Subject says why in brief; body adds context.
- One logical change per commit. Do not bundle unrelated work.

**Types:** `feat` (user-facing entry or capability), `fix`, `docs`, `build`, `ci`, `test`, `refactor`, `chore`. Optional scope: `catalog`, `docs`, `toolbox`, `cursor`, `build`.

```text
# BAD — not conventional, too long, past tense
Updated the floating point tutorial and also fixed cmake and reformatted docs.

# GOOD
feat(catalog): add floating-point tutorial

Fill planned spine item 04 with a vertical slice: code,
README, catalog row, and a docs page that literalincludes
the source.
```

Do not use `--no-verify`. Do not amend a commit that is already on the remote.
